[SPEAKER_02]: If you're taking up nāma-rūpa, you undermine that permanence by seeing it dependent simultaneously while you are still holding it, up on viññāṇa.

360
00:27:50,256 --> 00:27:52,757
[SPEAKER_02]: If taking viññāṇa, you see it's simultaneously dependent upon nāma-rūpa.

361
00:27:54,378 --> 00:27:55,159
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's either-or.

362
00:27:55,379 --> 00:27:59,302
[SPEAKER_02]: There is no in-between, or left or right, where you can step aside and then look at both.

363
00:28:01,143 --> 00:28:06,346
[SPEAKER_02]: So, either this is determined by nāma-rūpa, viññāṇa, or it's viññāṇa determining nāma-rūpa.

364
00:28:06,426 --> 00:28:07,627
[SPEAKER_02]: That's your experience, always.

365
00:28:08,227 --> 00:28:08,848
[SPEAKER_02]: Why not the other?

366
00:28:10,763 --> 00:28:20,386
[SPEAKER_02]: So, by recognizing this general, in the particular actual body, you will be start, like, not knowingly in the beginning, but you will be ambit in those principles.

367
00:28:20,426 --> 00:28:32,451
[SPEAKER_02]: And actually, you can even continue the reflection, as I just started saying, you wouldn't be aware of anything, no matter how general or particular, if your body is not alive here.

368
00:28:33,371 --> 00:28:38,293
[SPEAKER_02]: Like the organs that you have no control over, your heart, your eyes, they're not there functioning.

369
00:28:39,343 --> 00:28:41,064
[SPEAKER_02]: Just your awareness will be inconceivable.

370
00:28:41,144 --> 00:28:42,065
[SPEAKER_02]: You won't be able to think.

371
00:28:43,286 --> 00:28:48,969
[SPEAKER_02]: At the same time, if there is no thinking of any kind, you wouldn't know those organs as organs.

372
00:28:49,590 --> 00:28:51,251
[SPEAKER_02]: You wouldn't know anything as anything.

373
00:28:52,271 --> 00:28:53,292
[SPEAKER_02]: It's just inconceivable.

374
00:28:54,113 --> 00:28:55,794
[SPEAKER_02]: Things without a name are inconceivable.

375
00:28:56,094 --> 00:28:57,035
[SPEAKER_02]: That's nāmarūpa.

376
00:28:57,555 --> 00:28:59,276
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, you can't have just rūpa, pure rūpa.

377
00:28:59,316 --> 00:28:59,476
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

378
00:28:59,536 --> 00:29:01,197
[SPEAKER_02]: You only can have nāma of the rūpa.

379
00:29:03,479 --> 00:29:04,639
[SPEAKER_01]: Nāma is...

380
00:29:06,209 --> 00:29:10,491
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you could say it's the all that appears, basically.

381
00:29:11,352 --> 00:29:16,214
[SPEAKER_02]: But the reason why it appears is because consciousness is out there with the rūpa.

382
00:29:16,374 --> 00:29:17,315
[SPEAKER_02]: But that's a different topic.

383
00:29:18,015 --> 00:29:28,941
[SPEAKER_02]: The point is, you can see your day-to-day mindfulness is fully dependent upon, like, random organs of your living body operating in their function, that you cannot control.

384
00:29:29,321 --> 00:29:30,542
[SPEAKER_02]: If that changes, you're dead.

385
00:29:32,342 --> 00:29:33,003
[SPEAKER_02]: And they will change.

386
00:29:34,177 --> 00:29:43,845
[SPEAKER_02]: So, at the same time, you are mindful, generally, and you're mindful of the very, like, undermining foundations of your own existence.

387
00:29:43,865 --> 00:29:52,852
[SPEAKER_02]: You realize, well, whatever I do, mindfully or unmindfully, aware or unaware, it's fully determined by these random organs they have no control over.

388
00:29:54,674 --> 00:30:01,760
[SPEAKER_02]: Then you might start thinking about the random organs as more fundamental, but then you realize, well, that's just my thought of that which a random organ is.

389
00:30:03,195 --> 00:30:03,835
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's your name.

390
00:30:04,256 --> 00:30:10,339
[SPEAKER_02]: Which means random organ would be inconceivable if there is not even a degree of awareness in regard to that.

391
00:30:11,419 --> 00:30:13,520
[SPEAKER_02]: If the name of an organ doesn't appear.

392
00:30:14,200 --> 00:30:17,942
[SPEAKER_02]: If it doesn't appear in experience as anything.

393
00:30:18,823 --> 00:30:20,924
[SPEAKER_02]: If something doesn't appear, you can't even conceive it.

394
00:30:21,984 --> 00:30:23,225
[SPEAKER_02]: You suddenly can't talk about it.

395
00:30:25,423 --> 00:30:34,007
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's enough to show you that, well, these random organs operate, but they wouldn't be operating if there is no consciousness in regard to them, if there is no awareness in regard to them.

396
00:30:34,807 --> 00:30:42,451
[SPEAKER_02]: So, I mean by that, even the living heart would not be living heart if there is no consciousness associated with the body as a unit.

397
00:30:44,292 --> 00:30:49,054
[SPEAKER_02]: So, in that sense, you start recognizing the consciousness is on the level of those random organs outside.

398
00:30:50,142 --> 00:30:56,527
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, below the threshold that you can see or perceive through any sense, it's the foundation of your senses.

399
00:30:57,628 --> 00:31:01,731
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's not in your head, or inside of you, or on this side, and then rūpa is on that side.

400
00:31:02,472 --> 00:31:09,998
[SPEAKER_02]: The rūpa and viññāṇa are there, and the kind of result of that is nāma, rūpa, viññāṇa.

401
00:31:10,518 --> 00:31:11,178
[SPEAKER_02]: Your experience.

402
00:31:11,419 --> 00:31:12,720
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, your experience, yeah.

403
00:31:13,560 --> 00:31:19,525
[SPEAKER_02]: But that's what I meant before when I said, well, whatever you think is your thought, or presentation.

404
00:31:20,825 --> 00:31:23,127
[SPEAKER_02]: Or phenomena, or dhamma, whatever you want to translate it.

405
00:31:24,649 --> 00:31:27,292
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's all you can ever have in regard to different things.

406
00:31:27,332 --> 00:31:29,153
[SPEAKER_02]: But even when you say different things, that's another thought.

407
00:31:30,034 --> 00:31:33,778
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you can never step outside of your mind and say, this is the real thing.

408
00:31:33,858 --> 00:31:33,998
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

409
00:31:34,018 --> 00:31:36,641
[SPEAKER_02]: That the real thing is known only because your mind knows it as such.

410
00:31:37,622 --> 00:31:42,146
[SPEAKER_02]: That's the priority of the mind, the first... the first verse of... of dhammapāda.

411
00:31:43,078 --> 00:31:45,539
[SPEAKER_02]: Mind is the forerunner of all things.

412
00:31:45,960 --> 00:31:47,080
[SPEAKER_02]: Structural forerunner.

413
00:31:47,340 --> 00:31:48,581
[SPEAKER_02]: It would be inconceivable.

414
00:31:49,182 --> 00:31:59,347
[SPEAKER_02]: So, when you talk about rūpa, or any other aggregate, you're talking through your mind, so to speak.

415
00:31:59,367 --> 00:32:06,672
[SPEAKER_02]: In other words, you have to know that when you say rūpa, when you say this, when you say that, that cannot stand for the actual elements.

416
00:32:08,273 --> 00:32:12,115
[SPEAKER_02]: Assuming that it does stand, means you conceive those elements in your thoughts.

417
00:32:13,203 --> 00:32:16,024
[SPEAKER_02]: Your thoughts are conceiving, and that's exactly mūḍha-pariyāya-sūtra.

418
00:32:17,685 --> 00:32:24,609
[SPEAKER_02]: Assuming the discrepancy of any kind, means you give them existence in your thoughts.

419
00:32:25,229 --> 00:32:32,133
[SPEAKER_02]: So, like, you know, the five codes of mastering your thoughts, and one who masters his thoughts all together, he's an arahant.

420
00:32:33,501 --> 00:32:38,684
[SPEAKER_02]: The danger there is, when you say thoughts, people think abstract, kind of theoretical, proliferating.

421
00:32:38,745 --> 00:32:39,105
[SPEAKER_02]: But no.

422
00:32:39,585 --> 00:32:42,487
[SPEAKER_02]: Looking at the door is a thought experience as well.

423
00:32:42,987 --> 00:32:47,270
[SPEAKER_02]: Now, another danger is becoming a... like falling into solipsism and thinking, oh, it's all in my head.

424
00:32:47,670 --> 00:32:52,814
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, a thought that things are in your head is another thought that is present, and that cannot be in your head.

425
00:32:53,434 --> 00:32:57,037
[SPEAKER_02]: So, a thought in my head, the space, this, opposite, that's all, again,

426
00:32:58,465 --> 00:33:02,007
[SPEAKER_02]: A phenomenon that has arisen on the level of the mind, which is where things arise.

427
00:33:02,127 --> 00:33:12,051
[SPEAKER_02]: Then, within that, you can distinguish different types of phenomena, but they all have things in common, which is, they share the same nature of appearing, manifesting.

428
00:33:12,872 --> 00:33:16,293
[SPEAKER_02]: And on that level, they're all phenomena, they're all phenomenological, which is why they're all dhamma.

429
00:33:16,794 --> 00:33:18,815
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, all of the aggregates are dhammas.

430
00:33:20,515 --> 00:33:21,176
[SPEAKER_02]: And saṅkharas.

431
00:33:22,296 --> 00:33:23,597
[SPEAKER_02]: Not at the same time, obviously, but

432
00:33:25,442 --> 00:33:29,844
[SPEAKER_02]: They serve as that which determines and that which is determined, depending on where your attention is.

433
00:33:31,244 --> 00:33:32,305
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't step outside of it.

434
00:33:33,305 --> 00:33:34,966
[SPEAKER_02]: That's why I said nāmarūpa, viññāṇa, nāmarūpa.

435
00:33:34,986 --> 00:33:35,846
[SPEAKER_02]: It's always either or.

436
00:33:37,147 --> 00:33:39,208
[SPEAKER_00]: So, every experience is...

437
00:33:40,141 --> 00:33:55,809
[SPEAKER_02]: Either nāmarūpa, viññāṇa, either two of them being combined or three of them... No, every experience, no, no, no, every experience, depending again on the approach, but in this sense, every experience is either founded upon nāmarūpa or either founded upon viññāṇa.

438
00:33:56,830 --> 00:33:58,210
[SPEAKER_02]: And by that I mean determined by.

439
00:34:01,892 --> 00:34:05,254
[SPEAKER_02]: As far as... You can't have nāmarūpa and viññāṇa equally in front of you.

440
00:34:05,834 --> 00:34:06,775
[SPEAKER_02]: You will be one of them.

441
00:34:07,690 --> 00:34:20,239
[SPEAKER_02]: Which means the other one can be, if seen correctly, can be the, the, the... Yeah, the undermining factor that will remove your sense of self.

442
00:34:21,740 --> 00:34:31,186
[SPEAKER_02]: If you see that my sense of self depends upon that which, right now, while I'm holding this, while this is me, depends fully upon that which is not me.

443
00:34:31,206 --> 00:34:36,470
[SPEAKER_02]: And actually, I just gave you the example, a rather general one, but it's a good start.

444
00:34:38,126 --> 00:34:42,650
[SPEAKER_02]: Your organs, your bodily organs.

445
00:34:42,670 --> 00:34:49,235
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, you have to bring down, you have to recognize the connection between the presence of a random working heart and your entire life.

446
00:34:51,016 --> 00:34:56,480
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, literally, working heart is like, like, like an object out there in the world.

447
00:34:58,302 --> 00:35:02,565
[SPEAKER_02]: But it's an object because of which the objects exist as phenomena.

448
00:35:03,644 --> 00:35:13,068
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's a particular type of object that enables your experience as such, because it's paired with consciousness, matter in consciousness, but none of which you can actually access or have an in.

449
00:35:14,569 --> 00:35:16,730
[SPEAKER_02]: So, control or input open.

450
00:35:17,610 --> 00:35:20,091
[SPEAKER_02]: They're utterly beyond, outside of your reach.

451
00:35:20,751 --> 00:35:26,134
[SPEAKER_02]: So, all you're going to have is a presentation, or their appearance, in a way.

452
00:35:26,982 --> 00:35:30,526
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you can know the direction they appeared from, but you can't, like, hold them.

453
00:35:30,546 --> 00:35:33,569
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't get... because if you would, arhanty would not be possible.

454
00:35:39,975 --> 00:35:49,725
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if the... if the... if the fundamentals, if the foundations of your experience would genuinely be within your reach, you would... there would be a self, there would be a creator, there would be at least somebody you can take the ownership of.

455
00:35:50,739 --> 00:36:00,982
[SPEAKER_02]: But there aren't, which is why, like... which is why the sense of self, or a vijja, or whatever else, it's completely unnecessary.

456
00:36:01,083 --> 00:36:03,023
[SPEAKER_02]: It's a parasite, is the only way to refer to it.

457
00:36:03,123 --> 00:36:08,145
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not, it's just... it can't be there, but not knowing that it can't be there, it's there.

458
00:36:10,966 --> 00:36:13,307
[SPEAKER_02]: There is no room for a vijja in the five aggregates.

459
00:36:15,627 --> 00:36:19,709
[SPEAKER_02]: Not knowing that there is no room for a vijja, not fully understanding what that means,

460
00:36:20,757 --> 00:36:37,728
[SPEAKER_02]: You make the rūpa.

461
00:36:39,128 --> 00:36:43,231
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, it's not like... it's not exactly an easy matter, but...

462
00:37:01,530 --> 00:37:18,240
[SPEAKER_02]: So, the good... the good way to start is, when you... when you take up a contemplation, you read the Sutta and the Five Agreements and be conscious of yourself, instead of trying to figure out what it all is, start by undoing what you think it all is.

463
00:37:19,339 --> 00:37:23,323
[SPEAKER_02]: In other words, nobody talks about nāra, or nā, or say nāmarūpa, viññāṇa, nāmarūpa.

464
00:37:23,343 --> 00:37:24,444
[SPEAKER_02]: They say, okay, it's nāmarūpa.

465
00:37:24,704 --> 00:37:32,211
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, before you can understand that, first, you have to purify what nāmarūpa designation stands for in your experience.

466
00:37:33,572 --> 00:37:35,274
[SPEAKER_02]: What consciousness stands for in your experience.

467
00:37:35,314 --> 00:37:43,021
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if you were to take up five aggregates and name them, in English, or Sinhala, or whatever, just repeat the name two or three times.

468
00:37:43,922 --> 00:37:45,343
[SPEAKER_02]: Do you know, at that time,

469
00:37:46,910 --> 00:37:54,156
[SPEAKER_02]: What that matter stands for in your experience, when you say, ah, matter, and see directly what that matter is.

470
00:37:54,196 --> 00:37:55,137
[SPEAKER_02]: And you realize you don't.

471
00:37:55,878 --> 00:38:05,726
[SPEAKER_02]: You take all of them and you realize you do use them, you do have some general notion of what they are, what they pretend to, but you don't actually understand what they are.

472
00:38:06,367 --> 00:38:09,650
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you realize the practice is completely the opposite direction you've been aiming at.

473
00:38:10,842 --> 00:38:11,962
[SPEAKER_02]: See, I'm trying to figure it all out.

474
00:38:11,982 --> 00:38:21,086
[SPEAKER_02]: You have to undo it, to the extent necessary, when the recognition of what they are takes place, based on the external instruction laid down by the Buddha.

475
00:38:22,566 --> 00:38:23,186
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, that's right.

476
00:38:23,226 --> 00:38:27,428
[SPEAKER_00]: Actually, a lot of dharma is based on stuff like

477
00:38:28,788 --> 00:38:30,149
[SPEAKER_00]: You say five aggregates.

478
00:38:30,409 --> 00:38:33,070
[SPEAKER_00]: I try to reach the five aggregates and I'm lost.

479
00:38:33,730 --> 00:38:35,671
[SPEAKER_00]: So now I'm trying to, you know, get them back.

480
00:38:35,691 --> 00:38:47,795
[SPEAKER_02]: So you take them, you can't change their order, so take them as they are, rūpa, vedanā, sañña, saṅkhāra, viññāṇa, and literally just a matter and then ponder.

481
00:38:48,135 --> 00:38:49,096
[SPEAKER_02]: What is that matter?

482
00:38:49,856 --> 00:38:51,937
[SPEAKER_02]: How would you describe it, even in your own terms?

483
00:38:54,108 --> 00:39:00,430
[SPEAKER_02]: Do you see that which matter is, in your experience, when you make utter designation matter?

484
00:39:01,450 --> 00:39:04,891
[SPEAKER_02]: Same for the feeling, same for the perception, same for the intention, same for the consciousness.

485
00:39:06,831 --> 00:39:10,492
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you keep drilling inwards, as opposed to building up outwards.

486
00:39:27,538 --> 00:39:38,325
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, you have to make it clean, accurate, in a sense whereby, when you read the sutta, when you read the five aggregates, you immediately see what there is in your experience.

487
00:39:38,345 --> 00:39:46,431
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't have to stop and think about it and bring... evoke the memory of what you thought once, which is why... how people became arahants just by listening to the Buddha once.

488
00:39:47,472 --> 00:39:48,893
[SPEAKER_02]: They knew exactly what he was talking about.

489
00:39:49,753 --> 00:39:55,054
[SPEAKER_02]: They didn't know the dhamma, but they knew, when he was speaking, what he was referring to, at the time.

490
00:39:55,794 --> 00:40:00,376
[SPEAKER_02]: So, by seeing those things, they are at the arahantship, at the full understanding.

491
00:40:02,636 --> 00:40:10,498
[SPEAKER_02]: So, the reason why we don't become arahants now, when you read the sutra, is because the terms that you read, you hold completely wrongly.

492
00:40:10,758 --> 00:40:14,599
[SPEAKER_02]: So, they don't actually pertain to that which they actually are.

493
00:40:16,938 --> 00:40:18,899
[SPEAKER_02]: If there would, you would arrive at understanding.

494
00:40:18,919 --> 00:40:19,339
[SPEAKER_02]: Inevitably.

495
00:40:19,359 --> 00:40:26,223
[SPEAKER_02]: That's why, like, correctly practicing dhamma has to result in... well, has to have the result.

496
00:40:27,904 --> 00:40:30,246
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't be correctly practicing and not arriving anywhere.

497
00:40:31,006 --> 00:40:31,726
[SPEAKER_02]: It just doesn't work.

498
00:40:33,147 --> 00:40:41,172
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if somebody tells you, I've been practicing dhamma 40 years, but it's not about becoming Sotāpanna and stuff, you turn away that moment and don't listen to what they say.

499
00:40:42,451 --> 00:40:51,314
[SPEAKER_02]: Because, actually, if somebody's been practicing for 40, 50, 60 years, and not even get the right view, it means they've been wasting their time for 60 years.

500
00:40:53,235 --> 00:41:00,538
[SPEAKER_02]: So, rather than presenting that as some sort of skill, as some sort of great achievement, you should be embarrassed.

501
00:41:00,558 --> 00:41:01,699
[SPEAKER_02]: And Ajahn Chah said the same.

502
00:41:01,759 --> 00:41:04,980
[SPEAKER_02]: If you're not solved the problem in the first five years, it means you're wasting your time.

503
00:41:08,380 --> 00:41:13,744
[SPEAKER_02]: And people are not, because they misdirect their efforts, or they don't have enough effort, or they don't bother in the first place, or whatever.

504
00:41:15,244 --> 00:41:21,489
[SPEAKER_02]: So, again, it all comes down, comes back to that self-transparency, like knowing for yourself, having that as a goal.

505
00:41:21,649 --> 00:41:25,891
[SPEAKER_02]: There's a reason the Buddha laid it down, explained it, and encouraged monks to contemplate.

506
00:41:25,951 --> 00:41:28,853
[SPEAKER_02]: If you were to understand what sotāpati is, you'll be a sotāpati.

507
00:41:29,994 --> 00:41:35,598
[SPEAKER_02]: If you were to understand what freedom from three first factors is, you'll be free from the three first factors.

508
00:41:36,471 --> 00:41:40,994
[SPEAKER_02]: There is no, like, discrepancy between understanding and then actually the reality of it.

509
00:41:41,034 --> 00:41:41,174
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

510
00:41:41,275 --> 00:41:43,016
[SPEAKER_02]: Understanding is the reality of it.

511
00:41:43,716 --> 00:41:48,680
[SPEAKER_02]: Obviously, it needs to be developed to the extent necessary, and then it gets fully understood.

512
00:42:00,203 --> 00:42:03,126
[SPEAKER_01]: So, like, you can't separate five aggregates.

513
00:42:03,386 --> 00:42:04,587
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't separate them.

514
00:42:04,927 --> 00:42:05,107
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

515
00:42:05,287 --> 00:42:06,468
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't change their order.

516
00:42:06,508 --> 00:42:07,709
[SPEAKER_02]: You can individually do it.

517
00:42:09,051 --> 00:42:14,795
[SPEAKER_02]: You can, you can individually be reviewing your designations of what you assume the five aggregates are.

518
00:42:15,956 --> 00:42:17,277
[SPEAKER_02]: But even that should be done in the order.

519
00:42:18,539 --> 00:42:19,399
[SPEAKER_02]: You start with the method.

520
00:42:22,102 --> 00:42:27,126
[SPEAKER_02]: And feeling in regard to that method, and perception in regard to the method, and your intentions in regard to the method.

521
00:42:28,158 --> 00:42:30,840
[SPEAKER_02]: Then, that which you think consciousness is, you guys will admit it.

522
00:42:32,941 --> 00:42:36,143
[SPEAKER_01]: Eric, in regards to admittance, you don't lose the sight of that?

523
00:42:36,163 --> 00:42:37,564
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't lose the sight, exactly.

524
00:42:37,704 --> 00:42:38,605
[SPEAKER_02]: That's how you keep the order.

525
00:42:38,665 --> 00:42:39,705
[SPEAKER_02]: That's how you affect them all.

526
00:42:40,106 --> 00:42:41,146
[SPEAKER_02]: Try a contemplation.

527
00:42:41,346 --> 00:42:42,567
[SPEAKER_01]: Understanding consciousness.

528
00:42:42,787 --> 00:42:43,768
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, exactly.

529
00:42:44,153 --> 00:42:47,556
[SPEAKER_02]: Because if you were to just take up Consciousness randomly, it means, oh, you're just assuming it now.

530
00:42:47,636 --> 00:42:52,800
[SPEAKER_02]: Again, through your own assumption, the Consciousness can stand randomly, independent of anything else.

531
00:42:52,860 --> 00:42:53,280
[SPEAKER_02]: It can't.

532
00:42:53,941 --> 00:42:58,264
[SPEAKER_02]: None of them can, which is why it's always the five heaps, the five aggari.

533
00:42:58,344 --> 00:43:00,946
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not, not, not two and three.

534
00:43:01,727 --> 00:43:04,789
[SPEAKER_02]: You can single out one of them while all of them are present.

535
00:43:06,510 --> 00:43:10,273
[SPEAKER_02]: So, on the basis of all of them, you can attend one or the other more particularly.

536
00:43:13,518 --> 00:43:16,620
[SPEAKER_01]: You're usually taking one of them.

537
00:43:16,760 --> 00:43:17,901
[SPEAKER_02]: One of them or all of them?

538
00:43:17,961 --> 00:43:19,001
[SPEAKER_02]: One of them.

539
00:43:27,086 --> 00:43:28,667
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's another thing you should start thinking.

540
00:43:28,707 --> 00:43:31,929
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, when you say five aggregates, it's not somewhere else.

541
00:43:33,230 --> 00:43:35,291
[SPEAKER_02]: So, I think, right now, I will speak your experience.

542
00:43:35,311 --> 00:43:36,512
[SPEAKER_02]: That's what five aggregates are.

543
00:43:37,032 --> 00:43:41,355
[SPEAKER_02]: So, instead of trying to, like, think about what they might be, you start looking.

544
00:43:42,415 --> 00:43:50,538
[SPEAKER_02]: In the general experience that you're mindful of right now, and discerning within that, because they're there.

545
00:43:50,558 --> 00:44:01,241
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if you forget that they're right here, right now, and go looking for them, even if you find something, that something will not be there because of which you started looking in the first place, because it was right there.

546
00:44:07,275 --> 00:44:24,166
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's what I mean, like, you start reviewing, you start basically learning how to discern, because you know, you were told, you have faith enough, that your experience as a whole, actual and peripheral, whatever else, whatever other approach you take, it's present right here, right now.

547
00:44:25,187 --> 00:44:26,107
[SPEAKER_02]: All, like, all of them.

548
00:44:26,127 --> 00:44:27,708
[SPEAKER_02]: Your experience is the five aggregates.

549
00:44:28,469 --> 00:44:31,671
[SPEAKER_02]: Any experience you had, any experience you have, will be the five aggregates.

550
00:44:32,919 --> 00:44:42,863
[SPEAKER_02]: And the Buddha said that when somebody recalls five lifetimes or five hundred lifetimes, what they'll recall is these five aggregates or one specifically unknown thing.

551
00:44:43,483 --> 00:44:44,403
[SPEAKER_02]: But that's it.

552
00:44:44,523 --> 00:44:45,264
[SPEAKER_02]: It's all within that.

553
00:44:50,586 --> 00:44:56,208
[SPEAKER_02]: So you start training yourself how to discern them within this mindful picture that you established for.

554
00:45:49,561 --> 00:45:51,501
[SPEAKER_00]: Matter is nāmarūpa.

555
00:45:52,082 --> 00:45:52,422
[SPEAKER_02]: Sorry?

556
00:45:52,742 --> 00:45:53,982
[SPEAKER_00]: Matter is nāmarūpa.

